WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
A session never breaks because the fiction failed. It breaks because reality intruded first. A tablet sleeps. A laptop wakes crooked.

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000
A player reconnects into a scene already moving.

3
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
NEXUS-PAN exists for that dangerous little gap between what the campaign knows and what the people at the table can trust.

4
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Presence has to be clear. Change has to be visible. Recovery has to feel calm enough that nobody mistakes panic for drama.

5
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
A reconnect should not become a rules argument. A conflict should surface before it hardens into table folklore.

6
00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Desktop, tablet, phone, remote night, train ride, home table, same campaign, same moment, no scavenger hunt for the current version.

7
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
For the GM, the promise is simple: can I trust what I am seeing right now.

8
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:20.000
For the player, it is even simpler: rejoin, catch up, answer the scene, stay in the run.

9
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:30.000
NEXUS-PAN is continuity with a pulse, built for crews who refuse to lose the night because one device blinked first.
